  "publicacion": {
    "titulo": "Nvidia's CEO quit. Here's what history says.",
    "descripcion": "Jensen Huang resigned as Nvidia's CEO on Nov 12, 2026, effective immediately, after reports tied him to an alleged Chinese spy. CFO Colette Kress is interim CEO. Nvidia, the top holding of the SPDR S&P 500 ETF, fell as much as 14% before closing down 4.34%.\n\nThe reflex is to sell when the genius leaves. When Steve Jobs resigned in 2011, Apple fell 5% after hours, and Tim Cook went on to lead the first $1 trillion U.S. company. When Jack Welch left GE in 2001, the stock fell nearly 30% under his successor by 2017 while the S&P 500 rose about 124%. Same panic, opposite endings.\n\nSources: Nvidia (Nov 12, 2026); CNBC (Nov 12, 2026); State Street SPY factsheet (Sep 30, 2026); Fortune (Aug 24, 2011; Jun 12, 2017). The spy claim is an allegation. Not financial advice.",
